From: Fedora/Cygwin
Subject: Keep .c files for debugging

Normally mkbuiltins generates .c files from .def files and then deletes
them after compilation. This patch removes the deletion step so the .c
files remain available for debuggers.

NOTE: This patch applies to builtins/Makefile.in which may not exist
in this repository (which appears to have been configured for WASM).
If Makefile.in exists, apply this patch. Otherwise, manually edit
the Makefile to remove any "$(RM) $*.c" lines.

--- a/builtins/Makefile.in
+++ b/builtins/Makefile.in
@@ -93,7 +93,6 @@
 	$(RM) $@
 	./$(MKBUILTINS) $(DIRECTDEFINE) $<
 	$(CC) -c $(CCFLAGS) $*.c || ( $(RM) $*.c ; exit 1 )
-	$(RM) $*.c
 
 # How to make a .c file from a .def file.
 .def.c:
